Here is a simple C++ program to control the GPIO pin 12 using the pigpio library on a Raspberry Pi 4B:
```
#include <pigpio.h>

#define GPIO_PIN 12  // Select GPIO pin 12

int main() {
  // Initialize the pigpio library
  if (pigpio_initialise() < 0) {
    printf("pigpio initialisation failed\n");
    return 1;
  }

  // Set the GPIO pin 12 as output
  pinMode(GPIO_PIN, PWM_OUTPUT);

  while (1) {
    // Set the GPIO pin 12 high
    gpioWrite(GPIO_PIN, 1);
    delay(500);  // Wait for 500ms

    // Set the GPIO pin 12 low
    gpioWrite(GPIO_PIN, 0);
    delay(500);  // Wait for 500ms
  }

  // Clean up
  pigpio_set_mode(GPIO_PIN, GPIO_INPUT);
  gpioterminate();
  return 0;
}
```
Let me explain what each part of the code does:

1. `#include <pigpio.h>`: Includes the pigpio library.
